{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Advances ONE accepted/in-progress kb.plan item by REASONING about it via agent.llm.tool_loop, and CLOSES the loop on completion. The human move_item to `accepted` is the authorization; the item's claim + FULL detail (never truncated - the 3000-char cap was removed 2026-10 so the whole plan rides every step prompt) is the GOAL. Gate: only accepted/in-progress entries are steppable. SUB-ITEMS: an entry other items point to via `parent` is a container - it refuses to step while any child is unfinished (children_open), so the loop drives the children; when the item that completes is a child and was the last unfinished sibling, its parent is marked `completed` in the SAME atomic journaled write (rolled_up_parent), so a parent is done only when all children are done. CONVERGENCE GUARD: prior steps = step_log length; at/over MAX_PLAN_STEPS it refuses with needs_reapproval until re-accepted. DONE requires a VERIFIED: evidence line or tool_loop parses it as IN_PROGRESS. The bounded final answer is journaled to step_log via patch_control_facet under base hash - on stale_base it aborts, never forces. base is the board hash from agent.plan.board. Returns action stepped|completed|blocked|step_failed|needs_reapproval|defer_stale|gated, loop_status, steps_taken/max_steps, rolled_up_parent.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opjijl1a158e0142bq1bd6","readers":[],"time":1792588553810,"username":"system","writers":[]}